"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[8129],{78129:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"inflyaciya-ssha-pce-avgust-stavka-frs","locale":"en","title":"US August inflation comes in below forecasts, but statistical revisions explain part of the slowdown","description":"US August inflation was 3.4% against a 3.7% forecast. The Fed is not cutting rates; markets merely see a lower 35% chance of an October increase. Why revisions explain part of the slowdown.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"The US Commerce Department published August inflation data on September 30, 2026. Prices rose by 3.4% over the year, below expectations of 3.7%. Excluding volatile food and energy, the increase was 3%, against a 3.3% forecast. This measure is called PCE and is the preferred gauge of the Federal Reserve, the US central bank. Its target is 2%."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"The figures immediately changed market expectations. In September, the Fed raised rates for the first time since 2023 to 3.75–4%. After the new data, the probability of another increase at the October 27–28 meeting fell from about 45% to 35%. This is not a pivot to cheap money: the Fed neither plans nor promises a rate cut. Markets are simply less certain that rates will rise again."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"But statistics created the slowdown excluding food and energy. The US Bureau of Economic Analysis changed how it calculates prices for legal services, software and investment management, recalculating data from 2021 under the new methodology. It resembles a shop changing its scales and recalculating old receipts: prices appear lower although the customer pays the same. Such a retrospective recalculation is called a revision. It reduced July inflation excluding food and energy by 0.36 points, from about 3.3% to 3%. Therefore, August\'s rate did not fall; it stayed unchanged."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"The US economy is not slowing meanwhile. Growth in the second quarter of 2026 was revised up from 1.5% to 2.2%, and August consumer spending grew at its fastest pace in a year. Minneapolis Fed President Neel Kashkari said inflation around 3% remains too high and has exceeded the target for more than 5 years. In his view, the new data barely changed that picture."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"Consequently, US loans have not become cheaper. The yield on 10-year US government bonds, a reference for mortgages, rose to about 5.3%. For Russia, the news acts through the dollar, which remains supported: US bonds pay more than 5%, so dollar money is still expensive. The official October 1 exchange rate is 83.56 rubles per dollar, 87 kopecks below the previous day. The ruble strengthened for domestic reasons: exporters sold foreign-currency earnings at quarter-end, while importers slowed activity before China\'s week-long holiday."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"What remains unknown is that August\'s data do not include September\'s fuel-price increases caused by the war with Iran; the next report could revive discussion of a rate increase. Dollar holders face a choice. Selling on the inflation slowdown means trusting a figure largely shaped by recalculation. Buying in anticipation of new rate increases means betting on a report nobody has yet seen."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"What was US inflation in August 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"The PCE index, the Fed\'s main reference, rose by 3.4% over the year versus a 3.7% forecast. Excluding food and energy, the figure was 3% versus a 3.3% forecast. The Fed\'s target is 2%."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"Will the Fed raise rates in October 2026?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"After the August data, markets estimate the probability at about 35%, down from 45% the previous day. The current Fed rate is 3.75–4%; the decision will be made on October 27–28."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"Why was US inflation below forecasts?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"Partly because of a methodological change. Statisticians recalculated prices for legal services, software and investment management from 2021. After revision, July inflation excluding food and energy fell by 0.36 points, from about 3.3% to 3%."}],"sources":[{"label":"Fed\'s preferred gauge showed core inflation at 3.0% in August","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/30/feds-preferred-gauge-showed-core-inflation-at-3point0percent-in-august-much-lighter-than-expected.html"},{"label":"Minneapolis Fed President Neel Kashkari interview","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/30/watch-minneapolis-fed-president-neel-kashkari.html"},{"label":"Good news in US inflation report boosts chances Fed won\'t hike rates","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/30/inflation-report-interest-rates-fed"},{"label":"PCE inflation eases to 3.4%, cooling the case for another Fed rate hike","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/article/pce-inflation-eases-to-34--cooling-the-case-for-another-fed-rate-hike-125513195.html"},{"label":"PCE price index revised down","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/articles/pce-price-index-revised-down-123741659.html"},{"label":"Fed\'s preferred inflation metric came in cooler","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/articles/feds-preferred-inflation-metric-came-163426036.html"},{"label":"Fed\'s preferred inflation gauge declined","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/articles/feds-preferred-inflation-gauge-declined-174601544.html"},{"label":"Fed preferred measure of inflation rose 3.4%","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/articles/fed-preferred-measure-inflation-rose-124249351.html"},{"label":"Gold steady after softer inflation data","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/commodities/articles/gold-steady-softer-inflation-data-000816044.html"},{"label":"Fed\'s Kashkari says inflation goes beyond oil prices","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/articles/feds-kashkari-says-inflation-goes-150738609.html"},{"label":"Official dollar exchange rate falls below 84 rubles","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/finance/news/2026/09/30/1233185-kurs-opustilsya"},{"label":"Dollar, euro and yuan exchange rates on October 1, 2026: why the ruble strengthened sharply","url":"https://www.vbr.ru/novosti/kursy-valyut/2026/09/30/kurs-valut-na-1-oktyabrya/"},{"label":"Meeting calendars and information","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomccalendars.htm"}],"sourceBodySha256":"1145a94c8144e6d38a235e40e919942738f6348f62bad69c60f81ff17dc4c1a0"}')}}]);